+# PROF-ON-02: fresh qualification
+
+Both lanes start with zero admissions. Historical accept-v4 ACCEPT.json and
+its replay command are OFF/P′ bound and must not be used for these artifacts.
+No files in historical acceptance directories are changed.
+
+Use the mature runner's exact source/tool/tree/config/target/stage checks and
+the accept-v2/v3 complete same-row inventory/regular-output/role gates first.
+Every failure, unsupported construct, unreachable/unknown property and emitted
+cover remains in the inventory. A negative must fail only its predeclared
+oracle; an additional uninit failure blocks its acceptance. Missing or partial
+receipts retain original exits/exceptions and UNKNOWN/NOT_RUN.
+
+`BINDING-SPEC.json` declares fresh source coordinates, targets, profiles,
+oracles, required covers and leaf dependencies for all 63 rows. Cover IDs are
+predictions only: they require fresh same-row function/site/status binding.
+All emitted covers must be SAT, including any additional covers not predicted
+here. A callback cover alone does not establish target return.
+
+`binding_v02.py` adapts hash-pinned accept-v4 binding functions to the new
+source sites, merge4 target and comparator factory. It checks all source-file
+hashes and row/oracle identities before binding. It is a binding component,
+not a complete artifact classifier: its caller must retain the earlier gates,
+fresh role reviews, source-chain verification and source/tool/config receipts.
+BOUND never means ACCEPTED. New uninit property roles remain UNKNOWN until
+independently resolved. Do not feed historical records to bind_fresh.
+
+The new closure's precise demangler rendering and the relocated frame's
+generated variable spelling are NOT_RUN. A mismatch fails closed and needs
+fresh exact binding; no renderer/ordinal guess grants admission. The frame
+criterion remains the captured counter write outside swap's two targets.
+
+Evaluate consumers after all matching leaves in each lane. In particular,
+profile_merge_consumer_u8_len4 requires accepted profile_merge4_contract_u8_len4,
+the exact LtU8/merge4_profile instance and an identical source/tool/config
+tuple. The old merge_contract_u8_n2_to4 cannot substitute for the new leaf.
+OFF and ON never satisfy one another's dependency gates. The general
+merge_profile 2..=32 obligation is unchanged.
+
+freeze_noncopy_n2 and rejects_always_true remain in both manifests with their
+original oracles, bounds and covers. Their ON qualification is BLOCKED_TOOL
+by the runtime PolymorphicIter route until fresh evidence establishes otherwise;
+the unsupported is not an expected negative and grants no proof credit.
+
+All preparation is STATIC / NOT_RUN; independent proof credit NONE.
